Context for fe979a6 (T035): MVP_SPEC.md section 8 states the selection rule the model checked: the host controls trusted profile files and selects one reviewed hash through its own review, and the qualification flag is not an authenticated approval. T028 had left exactly one clause unwired, and the model record left one open decision: the gate clause 'selected = p' had no registry code, and reusing qualification_insufficient would have lied about the defect (the profile may be perfectly validated; the host just stated no reviewed hash, or stated another artifact's). So the code profile_not_selected entered the registry through the permitted additive change, with the contracts README table, the repo reason-code list, and the states.json rows updated in the same change, as the freeze requires. The gate order matters for honest messages: scope, then qualification, then selection, so an unvalidated profile still reports qualification_insufficient with no selection stated (which kept the existing exploration and run tests green), and a validated profile with a foreign scope reports scope_mismatch even when selected. The wrapper could have taken the selection at load time, but per-run placement makes mode and selection travel together and impossible to forget: the run itself refuses without selectedProfileHash, and each enforcement request states its own selection, which is also what proves no sticky selection exists. The exact-only synthesized profile is enforcement-gated too: the contracts already said the host still selects the reviewed hash, and reviewer.profile exposes its content_hash for that. One gap stays honest in the tests: the evaluate API is T044, so evaluation admission is covered as the shadow admission it will reuse (every qualification status admitted), stated in the test names and comments rather than through an operation that does not exist yet. The changed resolved model stays a fixture/native-level row because the wrapper builds no live resolved_model entry; that comparison fires when an adapter states one, as the Jev adapter path grows.
